  "title": "Brain-wide human sEEG during aversive eyepuffs and ketamine infusion (Kauvar, Richman, Liu et al. 2025; DANDI 001347)",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from seven adult epilepsy patients undergoing extended clinical monitoring at Stanford Hospital, acquired during brief aversive air puffs to the eye and around a 40-minute ketamine infusion (0.5 mg/kg). This BIDS-iEEG derivative converts the authors' NWB release (DANDI 001347) to BrainVision format in microvolts. The recordings are 20-minute windows downsampled to 200 Hz, with contacts labelled anatomically but without coordinates. The data support study of brain-wide emotional responses to sensory experience and their modulation by a dissociative drug.",
  "methods_description": "sEEG was recorded with a Nihon Kohden JE-120 amplifier from AdTech platinum depth electrodes placed for clinical reasons. Signals were low-pass filtered with an FIR anti-aliasing filter and downsampled to 200 Hz. Each session was cut to a 20-minute window, with the eyepuff series starting 10 minutes in. Values were scaled to microvolts and written as float32 BrainVision files, with no further filtering or re-referencing.",
